      "text": "Entities:\n\nUser\n-----\nid (PK)\nlogin\npassword\n\n\nUserCategory\n---------------\nid (PK)\nuserId (FK → User.id)\nname\n\n\nUserSubcategory\n-----------------\nid (PK)\nuserId (FK → User.id)\ncategoryId (FK → UserCategory.id)\nname\n\n\nUserPaymentType\n----------------\nid (PK)\nuserId (FK → User.id)\nname\n\n\nExpense\n--------\nid (PK)\nuserId (FK → User.id)\ndate\nvalue\ncomment\ncategoryId (FK → UserCategory.id)\nsubcategoryId (FK → UserSubcategory.id)\npaymentTypeId (FK → UserPaymentType.id)\n\n------------------------------------------------------\nRelationships:\n\nOne User can have many Expenses, but each Expense belongs to exactly one User. (1:N)\nOne User can have many UserPaymentTypes, but each UserPaymentType belongs to exactly one User. (1:N)\nOne User can have many UserCategories, but each UserCategory belongs to exactly one User. (1:N)\nOne User can have many UserSubCategories, but each UserSubCategory belongs to exactly one User. (1:N)\nOne UserCategory can have many UserSubCategories, but each UserSubCategory belongs to exactly one UserCategory. (1:N)\n\nEach Expense has exactly one UserCategory, but each UserCategory can be associated with many Expenses. (N:1)\nEach Expense has exactly one UserSubCategory, but each UserSubCategory can be associated with many Expenses. (N:1)\nEach Expense has exactly one UserPaymentType, but each UserPaymentType can be associated with many Expenses. (N:1)\n\n------------------------------------------------------\nConstraints:\nEach UserSubCategory belongs to exactly one UserCategory, and each Expense must reference a UserSubCategory that belongs to the referenced UserCategory.\nEach Expense must reference only UserCategories, UserSubCategories, and UserPaymentTypes that belong to the same User as the Expense.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Entities:\n\nUser\n-----\nid (PK)\nlogin\npassword\n\n\nUserCategory\n---------------\nid (PK)\nuserId (FK → User.id)\nname\n\n\nUserSubcategory\n-----------------\nid (PK)\nuserId (FK → User.id)\ncategoryId (FK → UserCategory.id)\nname\n\n\nUserPaymentType\n----------------\nid (PK)\nuserId (FK → User.id)\nname\n\n\nExpense\n--------\nid (PK)\nuserId (FK → User.id)\ndate\nvalue\ncomment\ncategoryId (FK → UserCategory.id)\nsubcategoryId (FK → UserSubcategory.id)\npaymentTypeId (FK → UserPaymentType.id)\n\n------------------------------------------------------\nRelationships:\n\nOne User can have many Expenses, but each Expense belongs to exactly one User. (1:N)\nOne User can have many UserPaymentTypes, but each UserPaymentType belongs to exactly one User. (1:N)\nOne User can have many UserCategories, but each UserCategory belongs to exactly one User. (1:N)\nOne User can have many UserSubCategories, but each UserSubCategory belongs to exactly one User. (1:N)\nOne UserCategory can have many UserSubCategories, but each UserSubCategory belongs to exactly one UserCategory. (1:N)\n\nEach Expense has exactly one UserCategory, but each UserCategory can be associated with many Expenses. (N:1)\nEach Expense has exactly one UserSubCategory, but each UserSubCategory can be associated with many Expenses. (N:1)\nEach Expense has exactly one UserPaymentType, but each UserPaymentType can be associated with many Expenses. (N:1)\n\n------------------------------------------------------\nConstraints:\nEach UserSubCategory belongs to exactly one UserCategory, and each Expense must reference a UserSubCategory that belongs to the referenced UserCategory.\nEach Expense must reference only UserCategories, UserSubCategories, and UserPaymentTypes that belong to the same User as the Expense.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
